block head
    title Dental Caries - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Dental Caries
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK551699/") National Library of Medicine]:
    blockquote Dental caries is a common chronic infectious resulting from tooth-adherent cariogenic bacteria, primarily Streptococcus Mutans, which metabolize sugars to produce acid, demineralizing the tooth structure over time.
